{title: Emaús}
{artist: Morada}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{c: intro}
[E] [G#m] [F#] [B/D#]
[E] [G#m] [F#]

{c: verse}
[E]Quem é esse que vem, nos abraçando [B]
WHO IS THIS ONE WHO COMES, EMBRACING US
[E]Quem é esse que vem
WHO IS THIS ONE WHO COMES
[B]Nos constrangendo com o [F#]olhar
OVERWHELMING US WITH HIS GAZE
[E]Ele é tão sábio ensina em [F#]amor
HE IS SO WISE, HE TEACHES WITH LOVE
[E]Ele é tão manso cuida dos [F#]corações
HE IS SO GENTLE, HE TENDS TO OUR HEARTS

{c: pre-chorus}
[E]Ele entrou em casa
HE HAS COME INTO THE HOUSE
[F#]Ele está à mesa
HE IS AT THE TABLE
[G#m]Ele nos observa
HE IS WATCHING OVER US
[F#/A#]Sabe que o esperamos
HE KNOWS WE HAVE BEEN WAITING FOR HIM

{c: chorus}
[C#m]E ao partir o pão os nossos olhos se [B/D#]abrem
AND AS HE BREAKS THE BREAD OUR EYES ARE OPENED
[E]E reconhecemos quem [F#]Tú és
AND WE RECOGNIZE WHO YOU ARE
[C#m]Ao som da Tua voz, os nossos [B/D#]corações
AT THE SOUND OF YOUR VOICE OUR HEARTS
[E]Queimam de amor, queimam de [F#]amor
BURN WITH LOVE, BURN WITH LOVE

{c: bridge}
[E]Nós arrumamos a casa [G#m]
WE HAVE TIDIED THE HOUSE
[F#]Perfumamos ela toda [B/D#]
WE HAVE FILLED IT WITH FRAGRANCE
[E]Nós preparamos a mesa [G#m]
WE HAVE PREPARED THE TABLE
[F#]Tome o lugar de honra [B/D#]
TAKE THE PLACE OF HONOR